items.body:
`if` statements run code only when a condition is `true`:

~~~
function describe(temp) {
  if (temp > 25) {
    return "hot";
  } else if (temp > 15) {
    return "nice";
  } else {
    return "cold";
  }
}
~~~

Comparison operators: `>` `<` `>=` `<=`, `===` (equal) and `!==` (not equal). Combine conditions with `&&` (and) or `||` (or).

Conditions are checked top to bottom, and the first one that's true wins.

