items.body:
An **array** is an ordered list of values:

~~~
const colors = ["red", "green", "blue"];
console.log(colors[0]);      // "red" (counting starts at 0!)
console.log(colors.length);  // 3
colors.push("purple");       // add to the end
~~~

Use `for...of` to loop over every item:

~~~
for (const color of colors) {
  console.log(color);
}
~~~

items.starter:
function largest(nums) {
  let biggest = nums[0];

  return biggest;
}

console.log(largest([3, 9, 2])); // 9

items.solution:
function largest(nums) {
  let biggest = nums[0];
  for (const n of nums) {
    if (n > biggest) {
      biggest = n;
    }
  }
  return biggest;
}

console.log(largest([3, 9, 2])); // 9

