A **variable** is a named box that stores a value. You can read it, use it and change it later.

~~~
let player = "Moo";
let score = 0;
score = score + 10;
console.log(player + " has " + score + " points");
~~~

`let` creates a variable. `=` puts a value into it. Text values (called **strings**) go in quotes; numbers don't.

