Programs choose what to do with **if / else**:

~~~
let hour = 20;
if (hour < 12) {
  console.log("Good morning");
} else {
  console.log("Good evening");
}
~~~

The condition inside `( )` is checked. If it's `true`, the first block runs; otherwise the `else` block runs. Use `>` `<` `>=` `<=` `===` to compare.

