A **loop** repeats code so you don't have to write it again and again.

~~~
for (let i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
  console.log("Lap " + i);
}
~~~

This `for` loop has three parts: **start** (`let i = 1`), **keep going while** (`i <= 3`) and **step** (`i++` adds 1). It logs Lap 1, Lap 2 and Lap 3.

