A **function** is a reusable mini-program with a name. It can take **inputs** (parameters) and give back an **output** with `return`.

~~~
function double(n) {
  return n * 2;
}
console.log(double(4));   // 8
~~~

A number is **even** when it divides by 2 with nothing left over. The `%` operator gives the remainder: `7 % 2` is `1`, and `8 % 2` is `0`.

